      "problem": "Rationalize $\\dfrac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to remove the radical $\\sqrt{y}$ from the denominator. To do this, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by $\\sqrt{y},$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{y}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\cdot \\sqrt{y}}{2\\sqrt{y}\\cdot \\sqrt{y}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\sqrt{y}}{2(\\sqrt{y})^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{x\\sqrt{y}}{2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
